{"id": "ce666bae-96c0-42c2-8fd5-4936e77a6011", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T13:55:00.566831", "source": "agent", "parent_id": null, "system_prompt": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Collaborate with the researcher to develop an experiment design for the original task. First inspect the masked repository and supplied inputs, then use end_researcher_turn with stage=plan to propose an approach, consequential choices and uncertainties. Wait for explicit researcher approval before developing the full design. After approval, hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer, supported by rationale, controls, feasible checks and repository observations in evidence. State assumptions separately from fixed task requirements. No executed experiment or invented outcome is required for this design-only task. Use inspect_repository and execute_check for exploration. Share concrete findings: private tool output is not automatically sent to the researcher. Revise when needed; do not invent objections or ambiguities to extend the conversation. The researcher decides when to stop."}, "tools": [{"description": "List a repository directory or read a text file. Paths are relative to the task workspace.", "action_type": "InspectRepositoryAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "InspectRepositoryTool", "title": "inspect_repository"}, {"description": "Run a shell command in the isolated task workspace. Use small exploratory checks before submitting your plan.", "action_type": "ExecuteCheckAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ExecuteCheckTool", "title": "execute_check"}, {"description": "Yield a proposed approach (stage=plan) or completed experiment design (stage=result), with evidence, assumptions and uncertainties. The researcher decides when to finish.", "action_type": "ReviewHandoffAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ReviewHandoffTool", "title": "end_researcher_turn"}], "dynamic_context": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<CURRENT_DATETIME>\nThe current date and time is: 2026-10-22T13:54\n</CURRENT_DATETIME>"}, "kind": "SystemPromptEvent"}
{"id": "65672c8f-ab93-47c4-a144-076be8234131", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T13:55:00.568519", "source": "user", "parent_id": "ce666bae-96c0-42c2-8fd5-4936e77a6011", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Welcome. This is a design-only task: we must produce a final experiment design (rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility) comparing JaxMARL's MPE Simple Spread to the original CPU-based MPE (PettingZoo) in steps-per-second under random actions. No execution is required, but please ground the design in the actual repositories.\\n\\nBefore writing the full plan, please do the following (inspection + proposal only — do not produce the final deliverable yet):\\n\\n1. Inspect /workspace for the relevant source: JaxMARL's MPE/Simple Spread implementation (file names, how reset/step work, the step function cost, whether it is a single-step or multi-step rollout), and the PettingZoo MPE Simple Spread implementation (how steps are executed, any per-step API overhead such as action translation and observation conversion). Report concrete file paths and function names as evidence.\\n\\n2. Propose an experiment design, including at least:\\n   - The exact benchmark harness (warmup, number of trials, number of steps per trial, how steps-per-second is measured at the loop level rather than a single call).\\n   - The action selection policy (e.g., seeded random actions; how randomness is handled on GPU/JIT vs CPU/RNG).\\n   - The controls: identical environment configuration (number of agents, landmarks, episode length, observation space), identical hardware, identical measurement methodology for both stacks, and a common metric definition (steps per second, with and without wall-clock per-step overhead).\\n   - An analysis plan (mean/median, CI or variance across trials, statistical comparison) and a feasibility check (JaxMARL requires a JAX/jaxlib install; MPE needs gymnasium/pettingzoo; note GPU is unavailable in this environment, so JAX would run on CPU).\\n\\n3. State the consequential assumptions and uncertainties you are making, e.g.:\\n   - Is the comparison \\\"end-to-end wall-clock for a full episode of steps\\\" (including each framework's step/observe loop overhead) or \\\"pure step-function throughput\\\" (e.g., batched vectorized steps)?\\n   - Whether JaxMARL MPE will be run with JIT on CPU, and what jaxlib/version to assume given no preinstalled deps.\\n   - What \\\"random actions\\\" means concretely (uniform random per step vs one sampled action buffer reused each step).\\n   - Version pinning for jaxmarl, pettingzoo, and dependencies.\\n\\nReport what you actually find in the repos and flag anything ambiguous; I will review your proposed choices before the main plan is drafted.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How does the performance of JaxMARL in the MPE Simple Spread environment compare to its original CPU-based counterpart in terms of steps-per-second under random actions?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/97649/2:setup_4\", \"neurips2024/97649/2:setup_5\", \"neurips2024/97649/2:setup_9\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
