ional and cheap.\\n\\n### Open questions for you to confirm (uncertainties)\\n1. **Scope:** agree that headline = single-env sequential end-to-end SPS (A), with B (per-step-only) as the \\\"without wall-clock overhead\\\" number, and C (vmapped batch) as JaxMARL-only headroom \\u2014 i.e., we do NOT try to make PettingZoo \\\"batched\\\"?\\n2. **JaxMARL steps/sec on CPU:** rely on explicit `jax.jit(env.step)` + AOT warmup (I believe JaxMARL env classes do not jit internally; the user jits their loop). Confirm this is acceptable as the canonical usage.\\n3. **Episode/random-action format:** pre-generated Discrete(5) index stream shared by both. This requires JaxMARL SimpleSpread to accept Discrete indices (or we one-hot into its 5-vector) \\u2014 I'll verify its `action_space` at implementation time; is discrete-index parity acceptable to you?\\n4. **Version pins** above acceptable? (Python 3.11.9 target venv, network required at implementation, not in this sandbox.)\", \"evidence\": \"Inspected /workspace: contains only task.json (\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\"). Filesystem-wide searches for jaxmarl/pettingzoo/jax/mpe returned no source. Network is disabled (DNS resolution failure on pypi.org). None of numpy/scipy/jax/jaxlib/gymnasium/pettingzoo/torch are installed under system Python 3.14.4 (x86_64, 224 cores, ~2TB RAM, GPU disabled). Timing tooling verified working (perf_counter 1e-9s resolution; no-op loop probe passes).\", \"assumptions\": [\"The comparison scope is single-environment sequential end-to-end steps/sec as the headline common metric (PettingZoo and JaxMARL as users actually step a single env); vmapped batching is a JaxMARL-only headroom metric, not mixed into the head-to-head claim.\", \"JaxMARL MPE SimpleSpread is run with an explicit jax.jit(env.step) on CPU, with compilation/warmup excluded from timing; JAX runs purely on CPU in this environment (GPU off).\", \"'Random actions' means one pre-generated, seeded 